I've already posted replies to Mike about this, but for the record...

>1) somas.sty was loaded from another directory rather than somas.cls from the
>current directory.

Yup.  Packages are called foo.sty rather than foo.cls.

>2) I then tried:

>%somas.sty
>\ProvidesPackage{somas}
>\DeclareOption*{%
>   \InputIfFileExists{\CurrentOption.clo}{}{\OptionNotUsed}%
>}
>\endinput

The option-handling code relies on the package-writer to include a
\ProcessOptions command.  In this case it should go just before the
\endinput.

It would be nice if the error-recovery for all this was nicer, but
that would probably add a large performance overhead, and people
grumble enough about speed as it is!

Alan.

